<title>LATVIA: Most Latvian T-bill rates dip at auction.</title>
<headline>Most Latvian T-bill rates dip at auction.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Most average yields at an auction of Latvian Treasury bills fell on Wednesday, maintaining a steady reduction of interest rates in the Latvian market, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The 28-day yield was the only one to rise. All amounts are</p>
<p>in millions of lats.</p>
<p> MATURITY  AV YIELD  LAST WEEK  NO OF BANKS  ISSUE  BID   SOLD</p>
<p> 28-day     4.50	3.95	   4	    0.75  1.15   0.75</p>
<p> 91-day     4.99	5.19	   7	    1.25  2.05   1.25</p>
<p> 182-day    5.43	5.63	  10	    2.0   3.50   2.0</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
